WEBVTT

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:08.540
I will Protect Chika!

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:08.540
Piyomon's Resolve

00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:07.060
I will Protect Chika!

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:08.540
Piyomon's Resolve!

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:12.840
Captain, after studying all of the Digimon crimes that have occurred,

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:14.500
I've come upon something very important.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:15.010
What?

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:19.020
There are seven emotions that lead the human heart towards evil.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:22.210
They are wrath, lust, gluttony, sloth,

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:24.620
envy, greed, and pride.

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:28.090
With the cooperation of Professor Stimson, who specializes in parapsychology,

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:33.010
it became clear to me that all of the Digimon who have appeared in the human world

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:36.340
acted violently because they were affected by these seven emotions.

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:43.290
Human emotions, huh?

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:47.660
But what's the reason behind the number of Digimon cases increasing?

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:49.250
I've already investigated that as well.

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:54.020
This is the dimensional wall that isolates the Digital World from the human world.

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:58.240
The right side shows how it looked like 10 years ago, while the left is what it looks like presently.

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:01.560
As you can see, the dimensional barrier is gradually breaking down.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:04.350
Furthermore, this isn't a natural effect.

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:07.270
So you think someone's doing it on purpose?

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:08.940
That hasn't been determined yet.

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:10.690
That's really useless...

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:13.650
Our sensors pick up a Digimon signal in Sector D, outside the city area!

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:15.380
Everyone, move out!

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:16.360
Roger!

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:23.800
Where's the Digimon signal?

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:25.580
At Point D-101.

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:28.340
Hey now...

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:29.370
This place is...

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.190
Masaru's house?

00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:34.570
Mom!

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:35.170
Chika!

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:37.210
Welcome back.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:39.990
What's wrong?

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.140
Mom... where did you get that egg?

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:44.350
Oh, this?

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:49.310
While I was bringing in the laundry, this came drifting down from the sky.

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:54.050
I thought Agu-chan would be delighted if I used it to make fried eggs.

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:57.030
That sounds so good...!

00:01:57.230 --> 00:01:58.780
What? A Digiegg?

00:01:58.780 --> 00:01:59.560
Yes.

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:01.330
Carry it back to HQ before it hatches.

00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:02.390
Handle with care.

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:03.690
Roger.

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:05.310
Hear that, Lalamon? Handle with care!

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:08.210
This is the sixth one.

00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:09.040
Yeah.

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:15.930
Until now, there were five cases where a Digimon appeared in the human world in its egg state.

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:21.110
They were Lalamon, Gaomon, PawnChessmon White and Black, and Agumon.

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:22.720
Oh, I'm the fifth one.

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:28.800
Digimon that hatch from their eggs need a partner who has a compatible Digisoul for them.

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:33.690
Both Yoshino-san and I were compatible, so we were scouted by DATS.

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:36.600
Anyway, let's transport this back to HQ quickly.

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:39.240
Tohma, don't drop it!

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:41.390
I-It wasn't me... I think it moved...

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:42.960
That's not possible!

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:44.900
It's moving!

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:46.890
Grab it, quick!

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:53.420
I've got it! Pile on!

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:00.850
Oh, wrong one.

00:03:00.850 --> 00:03:01.680
You're terrible.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:03.240
It's over here.

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:04.550
I got it!

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:21.700
Puwamon

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:21.700
Baby Level

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:15.750
Puwamon.

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:18.810
A Baby Level Digimon covered with soft plumage.

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:21.700
It is very curious and becomes easily attached to people.

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:26.160
IT'S SO CUTE!

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:38.410
There, there.

00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:39.880
Drink well.

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:42.510
Puwamon

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:41.540
Puwamon.

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:45.890
Although clingy, it extremely hates having its tail touched.

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:49.070
Tell me that sooner!

00:03:51.470 --> 00:03:53.960
Let's take it back to HQ already.

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:56.730
No. Now that it's hatched, we can't reposition it like this.

00:03:57.550 --> 00:04:00.540
Digimon are easily influenced by human emotions.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.880
I'm concerned that it'll run rampant during transportation.

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:03.530
Oh no...

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:05.510
Then what do you want us to do?

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:06.660
Leave it to me.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:08.240
Yes, Master.

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:09.880
What's this?

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:13.290
A Desire-Hunting Generating Device which I invented.

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:15.990
It can quarantine against human emotions.

00:04:16.850 --> 00:04:18.870
We can't eat dinner with this thing in here!

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:20.810
What is he doing?

00:04:24.050 --> 00:04:26.170
What? You want some?

00:04:26.170 --> 00:04:26.800
Here.

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:29.010
Here.

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:32.890
Agu-chan!

00:04:33.730 --> 00:04:37.130
Puwamon is still a baby, so don't bully him!

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:38.360
Okay, I'm sorry...

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:39.690
No, I'm not bullying him!

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:42.720
That's right, I have to give you a name.

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:44.880
Because you're Puwamon, I should use Puu...

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:46.290
I got it! Puu-chan!

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:48.830
What?

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:52.330
I'm supposed to be the idol in the Daimon family!

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:53.360
Puu!

00:04:55.490 --> 00:04:56.170
Puu!

00:04:56.830 --> 00:04:57.410
Puu!

00:04:57.410 --> 00:04:58.330
Puu! Puu!

00:05:00.010 --> 00:05:01.850
What's that? Is he copying Puwamon?

00:05:01.850 --> 00:05:03.560
He doesn't look like him at all!

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:05.150
Especially when he's eating.

00:05:08.210 --> 00:05:09.540
Take care of the rest.

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:10.600
Sure.

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:12.330
Where's Puwamon?

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:14.060
It's with Chika-chan.

00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:15.730
Sleeping

00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:19.690
♪  There's a voice singing a lullabye... ♪

00:05:30.890 --> 00:05:32.870
So this is the human world...

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:47.320
Here you go.

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:48.510
Oh, please don't take the trouble.

00:05:48.510 --> 00:05:51.090
How long are you gonna keep this up?

00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:53.920
This device still needs some fine-tuning.

00:05:55.530 --> 00:05:58.060
So you've turned out this useless junk.

00:05:58.060 --> 00:05:59.390
What are you trying to say?

00:05:59.390 --> 00:06:00.910
I'll take a look.

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:01.400
No way!

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:03.270
Oh c'mon! It's not a big deal!

00:06:03.270 --> 00:06:04.640
Stop! Don't touch it!

00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:05.660
C'mon!

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:06.280
My, my.

00:06:05.730 --> 00:06:06.720
You'll break it!

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:07.690
Mom!

00:06:08.980 --> 00:06:10.310
What's wrong?

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:13.410
Look, you woke her up!

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:15.000
Wh-What's wrong, Chika?

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:16.240
Masaru-niichan!

00:06:16.690 --> 00:06:18.040
It's Puu-chan...

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:21.620
It's been acting really frightened of something for a while...

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:23.890
Hey, come out!

00:06:23.890 --> 00:06:25.420
What are you doing?

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:28.080
I can't sleep because you're so loud!

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:31.130
What's going on?

00:06:31.420 --> 00:06:32.600
Agu-chan...

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:33.410
Huh?

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:34.950
So you're the culprit.

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:38.060
We'll listen to all the excuses you've got downstairs.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:38.500
I wasn't bullying 'im!

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:40.360
I'm an idol!

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:42.160
Let go of me!

00:06:43.480 --> 00:06:44.240
Now then.

00:06:44.930 --> 00:06:46.560
Puu-chan, come out.

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:47.760
The evil's gone now.

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:52.580
No...

00:06:52.580 --> 00:06:55.030
It's not Agumon that he's scared of...

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:05.680
Who the hell are you?!

00:07:05.680 --> 00:07:06.980
Where's the egg?

00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:07.300
Huh?

00:07:08.410 --> 00:07:09.800
Give back the egg!

00:07:09.970 --> 00:07:19.770
Falcomon

00:07:09.970 --> 00:07:19.770
Child Level

00:07:10.850 --> 00:07:11.920
Falcomon.

00:07:11.920 --> 00:07:15.190
A Child Level Digimon with sturdy wings that let him glide through the heavens.

00:07:15.190 --> 00:07:19.770
His special attacks are Scratch Smash and Shuririnken. He acts like a ninja.

00:07:20.810 --> 00:07:21.770
Puu-chan!

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:23.180
That's...!

00:07:23.700 --> 00:07:26.110
Did that Puwamon come from the egg?!

00:07:26.930 --> 00:07:28.570
Calm down, Puu-chan!

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:30.290
So what if it did?!

00:07:31.830 --> 00:07:33.490
Hand over that Digimon!

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:34.990
Mom! Chika!

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:36.500
Don't interfere!

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:40.440
Masaru!

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:41.580
Now, hand it over!

00:07:44.590 --> 00:07:45.750
You bastard...!

00:07:46.130 --> 00:07:46.710
I can't get out!

00:07:47.210 --> 00:07:48.070
C'mon!

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:48.650
No!

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:49.920
Who are you?!

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:52.130
Can't you see you're scaring Puu-chan?

00:07:52.130 --> 00:07:53.130
Go away!

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:55.120
If you won't give him to me...

00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:02.430
Puwamon...?

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:07.110
What's going on?

00:08:07.110 --> 00:08:07.810
A Digimon!

00:08:09.410 --> 00:08:10.150
What?

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:13.200
Damn it! I didn't know they had Digimon friends...

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:16.000
He got away...

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:17.890
What's going on? What happened?

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:19.160
You're late.

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:20.480
Puu-chan?

00:08:25.130 --> 00:08:26.120
I'm Piyomon.

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:27.430
It talked.

00:08:27.430 --> 00:08:29.160
You see how I got bigger?

00:08:29.160 --> 00:08:31.870
I did it to protect you!

00:08:32.090 --> 00:08:40.890
Piyomon

00:08:32.090 --> 00:08:40.890
Child Level

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:33.650
Piyomon.

00:08:33.650 --> 00:08:36.930
A Child Level Digimon whose wings are shaped like arms.

00:08:36.930 --> 00:08:40.890
His special attack is Magical Fire. He shoots out an illusionary green flame!

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:43.070
Nice to meet you, Chika.

00:08:45.840 --> 00:08:47.600
Nice to meet you, Piyomon!

00:10:10.470 --> 00:10:11.690
Mercurimon-sama!

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:13.270
Mercurimon-sama!

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:21.240
Gotsumon

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:21.240
Child Level

00:10:13.990 --> 00:10:14.840
Gotsumon.

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:17.590
A Child Level Digimon whose body is as hard as jewels.

00:10:17.590 --> 00:10:21.240
His special attack is Angry Rock. He can shoot out rocks from his head.

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:26.090
I've received news that Falcomon has gone to the human world!

00:10:26.090 --> 00:10:27.100
What?

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:32.670
He must have been very worried about the egg that was swept away by the storm the other day.

00:10:32.910 --> 00:10:34.520
What a fool!

00:10:34.520 --> 00:10:38.670
After I told him so many times not to get involved with the humans, he ignored me!

00:10:38.670 --> 00:10:40.310
What is Ikuto doing?

00:10:40.970 --> 00:10:43.370
I haven't an idea, none at all.

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:46.670
I can't even begin to conceive what that boy is thinking.

00:10:48.450 --> 00:10:50.540
Mercurimon-sama? Where are you headed?

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:51.990
Isn't it obvious?

00:10:52.660 --> 00:10:54.530
I'm off to bring back Falcomon.

00:10:55.110 --> 00:10:55.960
It can't be...

00:10:55.960 --> 00:10:58.660
Mercurimon-sama, you yourself are going to the human world...?!

00:11:02.110 --> 00:11:03.490
No!!!

00:11:04.060 --> 00:11:06.040
Stop! Let go of me!

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:07.200
Please calm down!

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:09.300
It'll be over soon.

00:11:09.300 --> 00:11:11.290
I'm not sick anywhere!

00:11:11.740 --> 00:11:12.540
Come now.

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:13.730
Piyomon!

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:14.460
Chika!

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:16.420
No!!!

00:11:16.520 --> 00:11:19.010
Chika!!!

00:11:22.340 --> 00:11:27.010
W-We were just examining her for a Digisoul!

00:11:27.010 --> 00:11:28.530
Chika's Digisoul?

00:11:29.360 --> 00:11:34.310
It's being speculated that Piyomon's rapid evolution is due to the effect of her Digisoul.

00:11:34.310 --> 00:11:35.060
That's why...

00:11:35.740 --> 00:11:37.920
We never asked for this examination!

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:38.820
Get outta here!

00:11:38.820 --> 00:11:40.440
It's Captain's orders.

00:11:40.440 --> 00:11:41.540
What?!

00:11:41.540 --> 00:11:43.830
Piyomon needs a partner.

00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:45.740
That's why we're inspecting Chika-chan.

00:11:46.050 --> 00:11:48.910
You want Chika to join DATS?!

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:50.580
That must be what the Captain has in mind.

00:11:53.380 --> 00:11:55.210
Stop making orders at your own convenience!

00:11:55.580 --> 00:11:56.870
But Masaru,

00:11:56.870 --> 00:11:59.240
you are also still very much a child.

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:02.370
I'm in DATS because I want to fight against strong guys!

00:12:02.370 --> 00:12:03.550
Chika is different!

00:12:03.990 --> 00:12:06.530
This place is too dangerous for her!

00:12:06.530 --> 00:12:08.370
Masaru, please stop.

00:12:11.030 --> 00:12:12.080
Mom?!

00:12:12.490 --> 00:12:15.100
Satsuma-san, it's been a long time.

00:12:16.620 --> 00:12:18.770
Are you here to discuss your daughter?

00:12:18.770 --> 00:12:19.450
Yes.

00:12:20.490 --> 00:12:23.390
I thought that with Masaru, it was inevitable.

00:12:23.390 --> 00:12:25.700
After all, he is the son of that man.

00:12:25.700 --> 00:12:29.680
It may have been a natural course of events that led to his enlistment into DATS.

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:30.980
But...

00:12:30.980 --> 00:12:32.770
Chika is just a little girl!

00:12:32.770 --> 00:12:35.750
Please, don't let Chika get involved in this!

00:12:37.960 --> 00:12:39.500
I'm scared.

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:43.630
It seems as though everyone close to me is being taken away by the Digimon...

00:12:46.690 --> 00:12:50.360
It's true that if Chika-chan's Digisoul is compatible with Piyomon's,

00:12:50.360 --> 00:12:52.810
she will be scouted into DATS.

00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:54.680
I know that.

00:12:54.680 --> 00:12:57.150
That's why I'm consulting with you.

00:12:57.540 --> 00:13:00.840
I understand how you feel about preventing her from fighting.

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:02.010
But...

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:06.150
Digimon who aren't maintained through DATS must be sent back to the Digital World.

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:07.860
Would you...

00:13:08.980 --> 00:13:12.340
Would you be able to tell Chika-chan to say goodbye to Piyomon forever?

00:13:19.340 --> 00:13:20.590
Hey, Piyomon.

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:23.610
What do you think will happen to us?

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:26.950
You'll stay...

00:13:27.900 --> 00:13:29.950
You'll always stay with me, right?

00:13:32.500 --> 00:13:33.330
Yeah.

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:34.420
I promise.

00:13:35.470 --> 00:13:38.330
No matter what happens, I'll be with you always.

00:13:38.700 --> 00:13:39.660
Piyomon...

00:13:41.320 --> 00:13:43.040
Piyomon, that hurts.

00:13:43.040 --> 00:13:44.240
Ahh, sorry!

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:46.020
It's okay.

00:13:46.890 --> 00:13:47.720
Thank you.

00:13:54.380 --> 00:13:58.090
Your back feels so nice and soft!

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:06.460
Let's step outside for a bit.

00:14:10.140 --> 00:14:11.370
Masaru-niichan...

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:18.440
What did you want to talk about?

00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:19.790
I'll get straight to the point.

00:14:19.790 --> 00:14:21.970
Go back to the Digital World.

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:24.120
Aniki!

00:14:24.930 --> 00:14:26.570
What if I said no?

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:29.030
I'll send you back by force.

00:14:29.490 --> 00:14:30.810
Masaru-niichan!

00:14:30.810 --> 00:14:33.210
This is a fight between men.

00:14:33.210 --> 00:14:34.820
Don't cut in!

00:14:35.380 --> 00:14:37.090
I made a promise!

00:14:37.090 --> 00:14:39.580
No matter what happens, I'll always be by Chika's side!

00:14:39.580 --> 00:14:41.090
That's why...

00:14:41.090 --> 00:14:43.250
I will fight you!

00:14:43.730 --> 00:14:45.250
Bring it then!

00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:46.960
Piyomon, don't!

00:14:50.380 --> 00:14:51.140
Here I go!

00:15:03.080 --> 00:15:04.050
What's this?

00:15:04.050 --> 00:15:05.150
You done for already?

00:15:06.690 --> 00:15:07.860
Piyomon!

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:10.450
Don't worry!

00:15:10.450 --> 00:15:12.480
I'm okay...!

00:15:26.080 --> 00:15:28.420
I made... a promise...

00:15:28.420 --> 00:15:30.550
With Chika... with Chika...!

00:15:30.640 --> 00:15:31.480
Stop!

00:15:31.480 --> 00:15:33.220
Don't fight anymore!

00:15:33.810 --> 00:15:36.530
Why does only Piyomon have to go back?!

00:15:36.530 --> 00:15:39.520
You have Agu-chan with you, Masaru-niichan!

00:15:39.690 --> 00:15:40.860
Chika!

00:15:40.860 --> 00:15:42.320
Let go!

00:15:42.320 --> 00:15:43.430
Look, Chika.

00:15:43.430 --> 00:15:45.820
Aniki's fists are crying.

00:15:45.820 --> 00:15:46.690
Huh?

00:15:46.690 --> 00:15:49.910
Aniki doesn't really want to fight either.

00:15:49.910 --> 00:15:51.700
But because he wants to protect you...

00:15:51.700 --> 00:15:54.210
Because he doesn't want you to get involved in battles...

00:15:54.210 --> 00:15:56.660
He has no choice but to fight with Piyomon.

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:01.770
Masaru-niichan...

00:16:02.460 --> 00:16:04.330
I...

00:16:04.330 --> 00:16:06.380
I will protect Chika!!

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:10.550
Aniki!

00:16:15.340 --> 00:16:16.640
It doesn't hurt.

00:16:17.470 --> 00:16:18.660
It doesn't hurt at all.

00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:21.040
You think you can protect Chika...

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:23.890
with puny fists like that?!

00:16:27.560 --> 00:16:30.280
Now I'll send you back to the world where you belong!

00:16:30.280 --> 00:16:31.530
Don't...!

00:16:31.990 --> 00:16:33.510
Agumon! Evolve!

00:16:33.510 --> 00:16:34.400
Okay!

00:16:35.770 --> 00:16:37.320
Digisoul...!

00:16:40.090 --> 00:16:40.970
What happened?

00:16:42.400 --> 00:16:43.330
It's him!

00:16:44.570 --> 00:16:46.380
I've come to help you, Piyomon.

00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:48.710
Now, come back to the Digital World with me!

00:16:49.090 --> 00:16:49.920
No!

00:16:51.060 --> 00:16:53.250
I want to be with Chika!

00:16:53.250 --> 00:16:55.000
Quit bothering me!

00:16:55.000 --> 00:16:56.160
Piyomon...

00:16:57.540 --> 00:16:59.330
Is it you?

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:01.200
Are you the one...

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:03.050
that made him turn strange?!

00:17:03.660 --> 00:17:06.050
It's your fault!!

00:17:09.920 --> 00:17:10.770
That guy...!

00:17:11.760 --> 00:17:12.980
Piyomon!

00:17:12.980 --> 00:17:13.920
See?

00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:14.990
I told you I'll protect you.

00:17:16.880 --> 00:17:18.240
That horned owl jerk...!

00:17:18.710 --> 00:17:20.440
Piyomon? Why?

00:17:20.440 --> 00:17:21.740
Hey, you!

00:17:21.740 --> 00:17:23.370
Get down here!

00:17:23.370 --> 00:17:24.990
I'll kick your ass this time!

00:17:25.550 --> 00:17:27.940
If you're not, I'm coming up there!

00:17:28.270 --> 00:17:29.960
Filthy human!!

00:17:37.210 --> 00:17:38.550
Baby Flame!

00:17:41.370 --> 00:17:42.370
Damn it!

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:45.420
Masaru!

00:17:48.220 --> 00:17:49.810
Is he the one that you saw yesterday?

00:17:49.810 --> 00:17:50.290
Yeah!

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:51.190
Stay on the alert!

00:17:51.720 --> 00:17:53.800
Gaomon, Realize!

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:55.360
Lalamon, Realize!

00:17:58.260 --> 00:17:59.300
Yes, Master!

00:18:00.040 --> 00:18:01.870
La~la~mon!

00:18:05.150 --> 00:18:07.900
Digisoul Charge!

00:18:10.780 --> 00:18:12.020
Gaomon, evolve!

00:18:15.250 --> 00:18:16.940
Gaogamon!

00:18:22.810 --> 00:18:24.330
Digisoul Charge!

00:18:28.030 --> 00:18:29.580
Lalamon, evolve!

00:18:33.440 --> 00:18:34.880
Sunflowmon!

00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:37.030
What?

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:38.980
Spiral Blow!

00:18:41.420 --> 00:18:42.390
What?

00:18:42.390 --> 00:18:43.400
He's fast!

00:18:43.400 --> 00:18:44.380
Sunflowmon!

00:18:44.380 --> 00:18:45.150
Yeah!

00:18:45.700 --> 00:18:46.750
Sunshine...!

00:18:48.080 --> 00:18:49.010
Sunshine...!

00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:51.780
Sunshine...!

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:54.240
Sunshine...!

00:18:57.370 --> 00:18:58.150
Sunshine...!

00:18:58.150 --> 00:19:00.170
You moron! Go on, keep wasting your time!

00:19:00.170 --> 00:19:02.590
Try saying that again when you're not looking like a fool yourself!

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:04.550
Now that it's come to this...

00:19:04.550 --> 00:19:05.300
What are you going to do?!

00:19:06.100 --> 00:19:07.270
Let me handle it!

00:19:07.780 --> 00:19:09.330
Piyomon!

00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:09.960
Masaru!

00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:11.090
No honorifics?

00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:13.980
NOTE: Piyomon calls Masaru by his first name, without -san, which is considered rude as they barely know each other.

00:19:11.090 --> 00:19:12.880
Get on my back!

00:19:12.880 --> 00:19:13.980
What?

00:19:15.350 --> 00:19:16.360
Hurry!

00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:18.300
Okay, get over here!

00:19:22.450 --> 00:19:23.740
Don't do this, Piyomon!

00:19:23.740 --> 00:19:25.370
I don't want to fight you!

00:19:26.220 --> 00:19:28.080
Even if you don't...

00:19:28.430 --> 00:19:30.100
We do!

00:19:30.510 --> 00:19:31.040
Ow!

00:19:31.110 --> 00:19:33.500
Eat fist!

00:19:38.300 --> 00:19:39.240
It's here!

00:19:45.060 --> 00:19:45.720
Thank you!

00:19:47.550 --> 00:19:51.430
Damn, I can't believe so many of those Digimon have sided with the humans...

00:19:51.970 --> 00:19:53.930
Don't overexert yourself anymore.

00:19:53.930 --> 00:19:55.370
I'm all right, Chika.

00:19:55.980 --> 00:19:57.380
Great job, Piyomon.

00:19:57.380 --> 00:19:58.510
Now leave the rest...

00:19:58.510 --> 00:19:59.800
to us!

00:20:01.900 --> 00:20:04.620
Digisoul Charge!

00:20:08.990 --> 00:20:10.790
Agumon, evolve!

00:20:14.520 --> 00:20:15.990
GeoGreymon!

00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:21.480
Mega Burst!

00:20:28.450 --> 00:20:30.470
The lightning canceled out the Mega Burst!

00:20:30.790 --> 00:20:32.320
Wh-What is that thing?

00:20:34.740 --> 00:20:36.320
Falcomon, stay back.

00:20:38.310 --> 00:20:40.500
A new Digimon signal has been confirmed!

00:20:40.500 --> 00:20:41.480
It's a really big one!

00:20:41.910 --> 00:20:43.280
Data analysis is unattainable!

00:20:43.730 --> 00:20:45.610
Analysis is unattainable?

00:21:07.390 --> 00:21:17.190
Mercurimon

00:21:07.390 --> 00:21:17.190
Ultimate
 Level

00:21:08.290 --> 00:21:09.550
Mercurimon.

00:21:09.550 --> 00:21:12.580
An Ultimate Level Digimon who boasts of being the fastest in the Digital World.

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:17.190
His special attack is Thousand Fist. He can unleash a super-barrage instantaneously.

00:21:17.620 --> 00:21:18.850
An Ultimate Level...

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:23.030
Masaru, Tohma, Yoshino!

00:21:23.030 --> 00:21:25.070
You won't be able to overpower this one.

00:21:25.070 --> 00:21:25.700
Retreat!

00:21:26.940 --> 00:21:31.660
You think the top street fighter, Daimon Masaru-sama, is gonna back down from this?

00:21:31.760 --> 00:21:32.780
Let's go!

